{"step_index":836,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:20:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-19T23:50:09+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-19T23:50:09+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/production_analyzer.py`\nTotal Lines: 238\nTotal Bytes: 9960\nShowing lines 1 to 75\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: Production-flow analyser.\n3: \n4: Reads Rockwell Arena simulation datasets (CSV, XLSX, XLS for Models 1–3) and applies\n5: Theory of Constraints (TOC) to identify bottleneck stations,\n6: quantify throughput gaps, and compare models.\n7: \"\"\"\n8: from __future__ import annotations\n9: \n10: import io\n11: import os\n12: import re\n13: from typing import Optional\n14: \n15: import numpy as np\n16: import pandas as pd\n17: \n18: from utils.constants import STATION_COLS, DEMAND_COLS, PARTS_COLS, PPH_COLS\n19: \n20: \n21: # ── Helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n22: \n23: def _find_col(df: pd.DataFrame, candidates: list[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n24:     \"\"\"Return the first candidate column name that exists in df (case-insensitive & stripped).\"\"\"\n25:     col_map = {str(c).strip().lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n26:     for c in candidates:\n27:         key = str(c).strip().lower()\n28:         if key in col_map:\n29:             return col_map[key]\n30:     return None\n31: \n32: \n33: def _safe_mean(series) -> float:\n34:     try:\n35:         return float(series.mean())\n36:     except Exception:\n37:         return 0.0\n38: \n39: \n40: # ── High-Efficiency Loading (CSV, XLSX, XLS) ──────────────────────────────────\n41: \n42: def load_dataset(file_or_path, max_sample_rows: int = 50000) -> tuple[pd.DataFrame | 